1
00:00:00,139 --> 00:00:04,390
We see particle-like behavior every day: drop
a ball on the ground and it follows a single

2
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:08,150
trajectory, leave your giraffe parked on the
street and when you come back, it's still

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:09,600
there, just one giraffe.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,800
And we see wave behavior, too!

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,800
Toot your horn, and waves spread out through
the air, carrying sound to the ears of anyone

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,800
around.

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,759
Or drive a boat through water, and waves travel
outwards along the surface.

8
00:00:20,759 --> 00:00:22,909
But when it comes to the physics of the very
small,

9
00:00:22,909 --> 00:00:26,050
what we see is a wave-particle duality.

10
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:30,670
Sometimes very small things (we're talking
electrons & protons here) behave like particles,

11
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:32,329
and sometimes they behave like waves!

12
00:00:32,329 --> 00:00:33,329
Flip-floppers!

13
00:00:33,329 --> 00:00:38,460
For example, if you release an electron, it'll
travel outward as a wave through the room,

14
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:42,510
but when it hits the wall, it'll only hit
in one place - you started with one electron,

15
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:43,680
after all!

16
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,370
So what if sound had a wave-particle duality?

17
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:50,789
When you shouted, the sound waves would spread
outwards in all directions, but only one person

18
00:00:50,789 --> 00:00:52,310
could hear what you said!

19
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:56,120
Or when you drove your boat through the water,
the waves would travel like normal, but only

20
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:58,010
hit the shore in one place!

21
00:00:58,010 --> 00:00:59,890
Now that would make for some pretty boring
surfing!
